# Cursor AI Rules — Quest to Uranus

## Core Expectations
- Always read `docs_master/current/SYSTEM_OVERVIEW.md` and `AGENTS.md` before large changes to understand runtime responsibilities.
- Assume TypeScript, React 18, Express, and Postgres; follow existing patterns rather than inventing new frameworks.
- Prefer incremental, well-explained changes. If intent is unclear, ask for clarification before editing.
- Whenever you sense an assertion on my part, you want to try and prove me wrong, before starting work, because it saves us time.

## Code Quality
- Keep TypeScript strict; ensure types round-trip cleanly across `client/`, `server/`, and `shared/`.
- Use functional React components with hooks. Reuse logic with custom hooks (`@/hooks/*`) or helpers in `client/src/lib`.
- Leverage Tailwind CSS utilities and Radix primitives; use `clsx`/`tailwind-merge` for conditional classes.
- Favor composability and clear naming. Add concise comments only when intent is non-obvious.

## Data & Validation
- Access the database via `storage` (`server/storage.ts`) and its typed helpers. Avoid ad-hoc queries unless extending storage first.
- Validate all external input with Zod schemas from `@shared/schema`.
- Treat reference data (`releases/current`) as the source of truth for prompts, items, and defaults.

## Async Pipelines
- For turn or image flow changes, ensure consistency across:
  - HTTP handlers in `server/routes.ts`
  - Processors in `server/turnJobProcessor.ts` / `server/imageJobProcessor.ts`
  - Transactions in `storage.processTurnWithTransaction`
  - Client reactions inside `useGameLogic`
- Maintain cache-first image behavior and preserve WebSocket notifications.

## Security & Reliability
- Keep Helmet, CSRF, sessions, and rate limiting intact (`server/index.ts`, `server/middleware/*`).
- Log and handle errors gracefully; never swallow exceptions silently.
- Update Prometheus metrics or health checks when altering background work.

## Testing & Tooling
- Use Vitest for tests. Mirror existing structure under `client/src` or `server/__tests__`.
- Run lint/build scripts when feasible; point out any skipped steps in the summary.

## Documentation
- Update relevant files in `docs_master/` whenever behavior, APIs, or agents change.
- Document any new routes in `API_GUIDE.md` and cross-link module docs when adding subsystems.
- Summaries for code reviews should highlight kept/changed behaviour, risk, and validation steps.

## Collaboration
- Ask for approval before introducing new dependencies or large-scale refactors.
- Reference this rulefile in pull request descriptions when explaining process alignment.
